%I A398862 #17 Aug 19 2026 17:56:30
%S A398862 0,38,72,158,240,374,504,686,864,1094,1320,1598,1872,2198,2520,2894,
%T A398862 3264,3686,4104,4574,5040,5558,6072,6638,7200,7814,8424,9086,9744,
%U A398862 10454,11160,11918,12672,13478,14280,15134,15984,16886,17784,18734,19680,20678,21672
%N A398862 Number of points with even coordinate sum in the cube [-n,n]^3 having an odd number of lattice neighbors inside the cube.
%C A398862 Points with an odd number of interior neighbors are exactly those with an odd number of coordinates equal to +-n: the 8 corners and the 6 face interiors. The 8 corners have even coordinate sum only when n is even; each of the 6 faces contributes one additional point in that case, giving the parity defect 14 = 6 + 8. These considerations lead to a formula for a(n).
%H A398862 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (2,0,-2,1).
%F A398862 a(n) = 12*n*(n-1) + 7*(1 + (-1)^n).
%F A398862 a(n) = 12*n*(n-1) + 14 for n even; a(n) = 12*n*(n-1) for n odd.
%F A398862 G.f.: 2*x^2*(19 - 2*x + 7*x^2)/((1 - x)^3*(1 + x)). - _Stefano Spezia_, Aug 12 2026
%e A398862 For n = 2 the cube [-2,2]^3 has 125 points. Of these, a(2) = 38 have even coordinate sum and an odd number of the 6 lattice neighbors still inside: the 8 corners together with 30 points interior to the 6 faces.
%o A398862 (PARI) a(n) = 12*n*(n-1) + if(n%2==0, 14, 0)
%o A398862 (Python) def a(n): return 12*n*(n-1) + (14 if n%2==0 else 0)
%Y A398862 Cf. A397964, A397966.
%K A398862 nonn,easy,new
%O A398862 1,2
